    "summary": "High‑energy Weather Report Suite and Dark Star→Morning Dew dominate",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a soaring Weather Report Suite > Let It Grow with jazzy horns, plus a smoking Dark Star → Morning Dew that showcases Jerry’s lyrical leads and Phil’s booming bass. China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider and a tight Playing In The Band round out an exceptionally high‑energy performance.",
    "review": "September 11, 1973 at William & Mary College Hall finds the Dead firing on all cylinders. After a punchy opener that includes The Promised Land and Loser, the first set builds momentum through a crisp China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider segue and an exuberant Playing In The Band. The second set lifts off with Let Me Sing Your Blues Away before diving into a masterful Weather Report Suite Prelude → Part 1 → Let It Grow, where Keith’s piano underpins jazzy horn accents without losing the band’s drive. Dark Star erupts with a thunderous bass solo and Jerry’s wah‑filled, mystical leads, seamlessly morphing into an emotionally charged Morning Dew that closes the night on a high note, followed by a rousing Sugar Magnolia. The soundboard source (gd73-09-11.sbd.lanum.184.sbeok.shnf) captures every nuance with crisp clarity, making this performance one of ’73’s most rewarding recordings.",
